// This strategy targets math-word-problem style outputs where arithmetic should
// appear inside `<<` ... `>>`. Outside constrained mode it generates freely,
// but it looks at the current logits and, when `<<` is competitive, it
// deliberately opens a constrained span in one step. Inside constrained mode it
// maintains `currentConstrainedOut` as exactly the text between delimiters and
// only appends parser-valid continuation tokens. If the constrained prefix is
// complete, it closes immediately with `>>`; otherwise it first tries a cheap
// argmax-valid path and falls back to the parser-aware constrained helper.
// EOS is terminal in every branch: once a step returns `eosToken`, the loop
// stops without any further append.
